  "pd": {
    "basis": "published-pre-1930",
    "detail": "First published in 1860 as 'I'll Twine Mid the Ringlets', music by Joseph Philbrick Webster, who died in 1875, to words by Maud Irving.",
    "sourceEdition": "Public-domain ABC transcription of the traditional 'Wildwood Flower', 4/4 in the key of D, ABB form, John Chambers ABC archive",
    "notes": "The tune is famous through the Carter Family's 1928 recording; what is encoded here is the traditional old-time setting of the 1860 composition, not that arrangement. Melody and changes only, no lyrics carried. The two-beat pickup that opens the first strain is kept at the end of the intro and at the end of the second strain."
  },
